IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc8-nouns`
IMPORT `roc8-order-37`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), Order 37: TESTS.  Every expected value is written from the text of the paragraph
-- named beside it, before running.  The "last day" is a made-up date standing in for O 3 r 3's count (S-T1).
-- The record tests are generated by work/mk37t.py: all limbs TRUE answers JUST TRUE, and each limb FALSE in turn answers
-- what the paragraph says (NOTHING for an owed limb, JUST TRUE for a limb not owed or met by its alternative).

`o 37 test d1` MEANS Date 1 3 2026
`o 37 test d10` MEANS Date 10 3 2026
`o 37 test d15` MEANS Date 15 3 2026
`o 37 test d16` MEANS Date 16 3 2026
`o 37 test d20` MEANS Date 20 3 2026
`o 37 test d22` MEANS Date 22 3 2026


GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A BOOLEAN, g IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A BOOLEAN, i IS A BOOLEAN, j IS A BOOLEAN, k IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `o 37 r 2(2) supporting affidavit`
`o 37 r 2(2) test affidavit` MEANS `o 37 r 2(2) supporting affidavit` WITH
    `o 37 r 2(2) it states the matters to the best of the information or belief of the deponent` IS a
    `o 37 r 2(2)(a) it states that the judgment is a foreign judgment within the meaning of section 2(1)` IS b
    `o 37 r 2(2)(b) it states that the judgment or that part has effect in the State of origin` IS c
    `o 37 r 2(2)(c) it states that the judgment or that part is enforceable in the State of origin` IS d
    `o 37 r 2(2)(d) it states that the exclusive choice of court agreement was concluded in a civil or commercial matter` IS e
    `o 37 r 2(2)(e)(i) it states that at the date of the application the foreign judgment, or the part, has not been satisfied` IS f
    `o 37 r 2(2)(e)(ii) it states the amount in respect of which, at the date of the application, the foreign judgment, or the part, remains unsatisfied` IS g
    `o 37 r 2(2)(f) it states that the foreign judgment does not relate to a matter mentioned in section 9 or 10` IS h
    `o 37 r 2(2)(g) it states that there are no circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court must refuse to recognise or enforce` IS i
    `o 37 r 2(2)(h) it states whether there are any circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce` IS j
    `o 37 r 2(2)(i) it states each reason why the Court should nevertheless recognise or enforce the judgment` IS k

