GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A BOOLEAN, g IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A BOOLEAN, i IS A BOOLEAN, j IS A BOOLEAN, k IS A BOOLEAN, l IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `o 37 r 3(2) supporting affidavit`
`o 37 r 3(2) test affidavit` MEANS `o 37 r 3(2) supporting affidavit` WITH
    `o 37 r 3(2) it states the matters to the best of the information or belief of the deponent` IS a
    `o 37 r 3(2)(a) it states that the contract is a judicial settlement within the meaning of section 2(1)` IS b
    `o 37 r 3(2)(b)(i) it states that the judicial settlement was approved by a chosen court designated in an exclusive choice of court agreement between the parties` IS c
    `o 37 r 3(2)(b)(ii) it states that the judicial settlement was concluded before the chosen court in the course of proceedings before that court` IS d
    `o 37 r 3(2)(c) it states that the judicial settlement, or the part, is enforceable in the same manner and to the same extent as a judgment in the State of origin` IS e
    `o 37 r 3(2)(d) it states that the exclusive choice of court agreement was concluded in a civil or commercial matter` IS f
    `o 37 r 3(2)(e)(i) it states that at the date of the application the judicial settlement, or the part, has not been satisfied` IS g
    `o 37 r 3(2)(e)(ii) it states the amount in respect of which, at the date of the application, the judicial settlement, or the part, remains unsatisfied` IS h
    `o 37 r 3(2)(f) it states that the judicial settlement does not relate to a matter mentioned in section 9 or 10` IS i
    `o 37 r 3(2)(g) it states that there are no circumstances mentioned in section 20(3) in which the Court must refuse to enforce` IS j
    `o 37 r 3(2)(h) it states whether there are any circumstances mentioned in section 20(4) in which the Court may refuse to enforce` IS k
    `o 37 r 3(2)(i) it states each reason why the Court should nevertheless enforce the judicial settlement` IS l

