-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 37 as regulative rules: traces`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A DEONTIC cannot be compared in an #ASSERT on main, so each trace carries the expected outcome on the line above
-- and work/trace-check.py (run by hand, on both builds) compares.  Day 0 is the day the period starts.


-- o 37 r 6(2)(b) the duty to serve the Court order: on the last day (day 28) the duty is met.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 37 r 6(2)(b) the duty to serve the Court order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 37 r 6(2) the applicant` DOES `o 37 r 6(2)(b) serve the Court order with a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement` AT 28

-- one day late.
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `o 37 r 6(2)(b) the duty to serve the Court order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 37 r 6(2) the applicant` DOES `o 37 r 6(2)(b) serve the Court order with a copy of the foreign judgment or judicial settlement` AT 29

-- nothing done by day 29.
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `o 37 r 6(2)(b) the duty to serve the Court order` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 29

-- o 37 r 6(5) the duty to file the affidavit of service: on the last day (day 14) the duty is met.
-- expect: FULFILLED
